  "id": "navigation/constructor_calls/06_conversion_casts",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "constructor_calls",
  "title": "Conversion casts",
  "summary": "A functional cast through a conversion function names the type",
  "prose": "`Target(source)`, when `Source` converts to `Target` with\n`operator Target()`, writes the type `Target`, which is the name of the\nconversion function too: the name leads to the class, and the\nparenthesis, as a C-style cast's does, to the conversion function.",
  "status": "supported",
